# ============================================================
# Exceptions — KEEP directory structure and documentation
# ============================================================
# .gitkeep files mark intentionally empty directories and ARE committed.
#
# Git cannot "un-ignore" a file whose parent directory is itself excluded
# by an opaque directory pattern (e.g. "data/processed/") — it never even
# traverses in to look. So real dataset content under data/ is ignored
# here using a *file*-matching pattern instead, which does not block
# traversal, and directory entries are explicitly re-included so Git will
# walk into them and find the specific .gitkeep exception. This is the
# actual enforcement for everything under data/ — the more specific
# patterns above are kept for documentation/clarity but this is what wins.
# Order matters: these three lines must stay in this order.
/data/**/*
!/data/**/
!/data/**/.gitkeep

!docs/**
!src/**
src/__pycache__/
